From 170f3bdbda097f5182d994828540c6dd5f21a470 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CustomKIMI <customkimi@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:20:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] customkimi: refresh CloseRouter model limits and
 endpoint efforts

At startup (and on the server's scheduled refresh), configured aliases whose endpoint is CloseRouter take context_length and max_output_tokens from GET /v1/models and the supported_reasoning_efforts of the endpoint they are actually called through (Chat Completions, Responses or Messages, following per-model base_url and protocol overrides) from GET /v1/models/{author}/{model}/endpoints. The catalog is never imported. Chat and Responses endpoints without a none effort become always_thinking so "off" is never offered or sent; Messages keeps native Anthropic thinking. Requests go only to api.closerouter.dev with redirects refused, are bounded (4 at once, 10 s each, 30 s total) and never put the key in a message. A provider's key is sent only when that provider itself points at CloseRouter; an alias that merely re-routes another provider there is skipped and reported. Failures keep the last-good values and are reported; metadata that would invalidate [secondary_model].default_effort is kept back and reported. The patch is merged into a freshly read config, only the models section is written, and [models."<alias>".overrides] are never touched. The TUI shows what changed and re-reads the active model's context limit and effort after a refresh, and its pre-session footer uses the effective limits.
